    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nI am using LazyVim with `mini.surround` and playing with it\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim test.html`\r\n2. \r\n```html\r\n<div>\r\n  <h1>Test</h1>\r\n  <div>\r\n    <p>Test</p>\r\n  </div>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n3. Place the cursor at first `<`\r\n4. `gzrtt`\r\n5. test\r\n6. Enter\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt should be replace the last `div` closing tag instead of the closest one. Which became\r\n```html\r\n<test>\r\n  <h1>Test</h1>\r\n  <div>\r\n    <p>Test</p>\r\n  </div>\r\n</test>\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n```html\r\n<test>\r\n  <h1>Test</h1>\r\n  <div>\r\n    <p>Test</p>\r\n  </test>\r\n</div>\r\n```",
    "closed_at": "2024-03-20T09:19:52Z",
