            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nIn 'mini.surround' the built-in input surroundings are searched with Lua patterns (similar to regular expressions). [Tag surrounding is no exception](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e025ee74705b04dd25a132a521c9c535dc78a8d8/doc/mini-surround.txt#L51-L53).\r\n\r\nThis particular case is because `<div>` tags are nested and similar to the 'mini.ai' tag textobject (for example, see #735).\r\n\r\nMy suggested solution is to use [tree-sitter based surrounding](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/e025ee74705b04dd25a132a521c9c535dc78a8d8/doc/mini-surround.txt#L732). This is the best option if you work in tag-related filetypes often and have tree-sitter enabled there. This requires investigation about which 'nvim-treesitter-textobjects' query corresponds to tags in the target filetype.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2024-03-20T09:19:52Z",
